Thank you for your Reply<br><br><br>Compare your DMR settings with the radio which works e.g. &gt; did that a couple Times even if the CP are different the settings seem to be the same. Also checked on repeaterbook for the Relais. Frequency, CC etc. are the same. I even created a new Zone where i copyed all Kontakts in, still nothing. I tried my other Radio to call the local parrot. Than i could her me talking, and Display showed my Name and DMR ID. The answer from the Parrot i did not receive on the DM-1701<br><br>There is also a possibility that the frequency calibrarion in your DM1701 is wrong &gt;&gt; i looked that up in the Manual. put the channel on 430 and 440MHZ, power on 5W. But i am not sure what i do with the value 184?<br><br>Also, check your Tx power (on FM) Power is on max. for now on all contacts. I can open Repeaters up to 35-40km away on FM. FM the Radio works fine.<br><br>To me it looks like the radio is not transmitting/receiving on DMR<br><br>CPS software is the version R2025.03.23.01, ( +DMR), and the installed FW on the Radio is 20240908143110 (9947546 D) CPU: TYT But this was the only FW i was able to install anyway.<br><br>The settings like DMR Filter, TS Filter, CC Scan.. i tried with different settings. I even reinstalled the Firmware.<br><br>Right now i dont have any idea what else to look for  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_confused.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":?" title="Confused"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8630">DA6VK</a> — Thu May 29, 2025 7:31 pm</p><hr />
